replies.text:
@HiddenCanada It's almost all hearsay from me. My dad told stories about him. I met him a few times as a young child and he scared hell out of me. He was a rancher from northern Saskatchewan who lost his land. He was a hard man of the soil and somewhat socially ungoverned. 
My dad said his dad supplied and organized sheep to be exposed to a blast or blasts. I was in my 30s when I learned that. I wish I was more interested then.
Regarding the Robson rainforest, It's like Being 500 meters east of Long beach, a kind of cool, moist terrarium with lichen, nurse trees and moss everywhere. The trees are coastal rainforest transplants.
